WEBVTT

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.600
Don't lose!  Don't give up!

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.030
Go, Hypnocorn!

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.460
Attack Rapid Warrior!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.510
Go!

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.910
Yusei!

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.270
Everyone led me to this final card!

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.410
I activate Stronghold Guardian's 
effect from my hand!

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.710
What's that card?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.820
By sending Stronghold Guardian to the 
graveyard, Rapid Warrior gains 1500 defense points!

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:21.130
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:26.660
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.140
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:36.940
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:41.910
There's no need to fear

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:49.590
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:55.590
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:01.370
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:06.770
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:14.850
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:47.090
Spoils After Battle

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.720
This means...

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.080
Can it be?

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.460
Yeah.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.900
We won!

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.580
We did it!

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.530
Incredible!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.510
They fought incredible battles 
to eliminate 12000 life points!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:25.140
The survivor still driving on the 
course is Team 5D's Yusei Fudo!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.820
He made a miraculous 
come-from-behind victory!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.190
Yusei!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.040
Yusei!

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.040
You did it, Yusei!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:45.980
Yusei!

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.270
Impressive!

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.430
That was a huge comeback, Yusei!

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.210
Yusei, thank you!

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.640
Are you okay, Jack?

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.210
Yeah!  You were so exciting 
that I forgot about the pain!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.250
Well done, Yusei.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.090
Jean...

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.140
We gave it our all in this match.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.880
Andore and Breo used all 
their strength to win.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.770
But at the very end, I forgot 
about winning for the team.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.090
I couldn't resist the 
temptation to challenge you.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.850
The strategist couldn't 
trust his own strategy.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.750
This isn't Team Unicorn's defeat.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.570
It's my defeat.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.760
Stop acting cool.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.950
Andore.  Breo.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.940
I'm sorry.  I wasted your efforts.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.370
It wasn't a waste.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.870
You had a new experience in this duel.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.390
A new experience?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.440
Jean, you finally met an opponent 
that you truly wanted to defeat.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.480
You're right.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.180
That's why I challenged you head-on.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:18.510
I never knew that as long as I gave it my 
all, I could feel this refreshed even in defeat.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:26.070
Yusei, any skilled duelist who meets 
you will want to challenge you head-on.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.300
Breo...

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.310
Thank you, Yusei.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.000
This duel will change my life forever.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:39.290
Jean, Andore and Breo, we also 
learned something important.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.280
We didn't know how to battle as a team.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:51.170
But by battling you, I think 
I know what real team play is.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:58.260
Exactly!  Team Unicorn, you were 
the most powerful team we've met!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.600
We fell for your strategies this time, 
but that won't happen next time!

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.570
I'm also going to become stronger!

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.660
We feel the same.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:13.050
The next time we battle, 
we'll definitely win.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:17.020
Let's battle with all our 
strength again next time!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:18.570
Yeah.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:25.430
Let's definitely meet in 
the finals, Team 5D's!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.940
Let's definitely meet in the finals.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:39.550
Definitely in the finals!

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:56.770
Cheers for Team 5D's first victory!

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:58.600
Cheers!

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:07.320
When Jack and Aki lost, I was really nervous!

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.970
Rua, what are you trying to say?

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:12.770
You're picking a fight during a party?

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.370
No, that's not what I meant.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.450
Stop.  There's no need to get angry.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.810
He was only telling the truth.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.400
What?

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:26.240
Since I couldn't participate, 
Team 5D's was a mess.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:28.870
You don't know the effort we put in!

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.480
You have no right to talk because you 
didn't participate due to a lame injury!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.180
A lame injury?

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.880
I was really worried about you!

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.280
Jack Atlas doesn't need 
you worrying about him!

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.650
Why does this happen?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.750
Because you said something unnecessary, Rua.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.280
C'mon Jack.  Don't be angry.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.760
That's right, Jack.  Let it go-

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.150
Wait, what are you doing here?

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:57.900
Your store is on the other side!

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.620
I'm off today!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.200
What about you?  Shouldn't 
you be reporting a story?

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.870
I'm reporting a story by 
investigating this D-Wheeler!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.940
You're doing more than investigating!

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.190
If you don't let him go, I'll 
arrest you for public indecency!

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.110
You're still here?

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.800
Go back to the Public Maintenance Department!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.210
I can't concentrate on my job 
when Master Atlas is hurt.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:24.350
How can you say that when you're 
in charge of protecting the city?

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.000
I'm going to write an article!

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.870
Go ahead and try!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.360
I'll squash that story!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.910
You're ignoring the freedom of the press?

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.610
I can't tell if we're friends or not.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.880
It's fine to enjoy our victory.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:44.130
Over the past year, we gave all 
our strength for this one victory.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.470
How special.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:51.930
Team 5D's throws a party 
just after one victory?

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.700
Sherry...

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.110
You're the person from before.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.710
What's with that arrogant girl?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.480
My name is Sherry LeBlanc.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.950
I see new faces.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:08.460
Sherry, did you finish your preliminaries?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:15.030
Yes.  Since you rejected me, Mizoguchi 
and I had to battle by ourselves.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:19.200
If it's just the two of you, that 
means you only have 8000 life points.

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.130
That probably caused her to lose.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.110
Sherry, you defeated all three by yourself?

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:29.820
What?

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.730
She defeated three duelists in 
conditions harsher than Yusei's?

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.810
No big deal.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:41.380
I have a goal that requires me to 
keep winning in this tournament.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.600
Do you mean Iliaster?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.800
Iliaster?

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:47.900
Did you find a lead?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:54.850
Not yet, but I learned that there's a connection 
between Iliaster and the Ghost that attacked you.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.310
Ghost?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.500
Do you mean Iliaster?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.790
Iliaster?

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.890
Did you find a lead?

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:22.840
Not yet, but I learned that there's a connection 
between Iliaster and the Ghost that attacked you.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:25.350
Ghost?

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:27.670
He's powerful.

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:34.280
His Meklord card is a Synchro killer.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:51.030
Iliaster was in control of Ghost?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:55.900
They're already around us.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:02.080
Oh yeah!  No one made a big deal out 
of it because the evidence vanished...

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.810
...but a guy named Luciano 
transferred to our school.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.520
His five monsters combined to 
form Meklord Emperor Skiel.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:28.920
Yeah!  The number 8 appeared, and 
we couldn't escape from the duel.

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:46.340
We took real damage during the duel.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.410
That also happened when my fake appeared.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:54.370
Real damage occurred then too.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.910
That fake was also a robot.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.580
And no evidence was left behind then too.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:29.610
Do these perfect humanoid 
robots actually exist?

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:33.660
It's hard to believe, but 
if you put all the stories

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:38.340
together, our enemy has technology 
that's beyond our imaginations.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.830
Like the factory we saw when our 
D-Wheel engine program was stolen.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:49.600
Yeah.  That factory was like a spaceship 
from a science fiction movie.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.380
Was it an Iliaster factory?

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:58.010
If so, what were they building?

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.180
Something that would use our engine program?

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.810
You didn't see anything?

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:09.180
A man wearing a white costume knocked me out.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.320
Sheesh...

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:11.670
Sorry.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.370
Why is Iliaster targeting us?

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:19.710
Because you're Signers.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.660
Sherry, you know the legend 
of the Crimson Dragon?

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.080
Of course.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:31.800
Did you think I would invite you 
to join my team without knowing?

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:35.730
Why are they targeting the Signers?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:40.110
Yeager!  That freaky clown 
must know something!

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:43.230
He's the one who stole our engine program!

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:48.440
Vice Director Yeager has taken a leave of 
absence, so he hasn't appeared recently.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.210
That punk is hiding!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.250
Maybe his boss knows something.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.890
Yeager's boss is the Director of 
the Public Maintenance Department.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:02.170
The new Director hasn't 
shown himself.  Who is it?

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:06.480
Three Directors have taken 
over for Director Godwin.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.870
Three?

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.230
Can we talk to them?

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:15.240
No one has met them, except 
for Vice Director Yeager.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:18.830
What?  That's weird!

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.790
You're right.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.480
Where are you going?

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:29.150
Like you said, I think it's 
worth talking to the Directors.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.770
Excuse me.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:34.060
Me too!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.040
It seems we're disturbing you.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:38.760
Will they be okay?

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:40.930
They don't know anything.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:45.320
We faced danger to go into the deepest 
section of the Public Maintenance Department.

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:47.840
You're talking about the bomb scare.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:51.310
What exactly happened at the 
Public Maintenance Department?

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.600
We were...

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:16.200
We went from the deepest section of the Public 
Maintenance Department to a completely different place.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.850
It wasn't an illusion.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:24.190
The man we met holds the key to everything.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:29.000
Is that man pulling the strings for Iliaster?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:32.490
I don't know.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:45.090
But if I keep winning in this tournament, 
I believe he'll come for me.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.750
Until then, I hope you won't 
become my enemy, Yusei.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:55.960
What do you mean?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.800
Let's meet again.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:07.810
Maybe Sherry doesn't want 
to battle against Team 5D's.

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.570
What Sherry just said...

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:15.540
Bruno?

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:18.510
What's wrong?  Are you okay?

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:20.090
Yeah.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:22.880
I was a little dizzy.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.510
I'm going outside for some fresh air.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.520
Yusei...

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:39.850
If I'm not mistaken, the inspiration 
I received at that time was...

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:43.480
Yusei, who are you?

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:53.490
If Sherry is correct and the people who 
control the Meklords appear again...

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.820
In your current state, 
you can't defeat Ghost.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:07.050
Unless you overcome your limits.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.640
My limits?

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:12.820
That's the only way to defeat him.

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:14.780
Come with me.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.990
Instead of telling you, it's 
quicker if you experience it.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.880
I'll teach you a new strategy 
that you know nothing about.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.750
Watch, Yusei!

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:28.060
This is the new battle 
technique to defeat Ghost!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.290
Accel Synchro!

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:30.760
Accel Synchro?

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.510
What happened?

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.430
What's that monster?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:01.900
It's the Accel Synchro Monster 
Tech Genus Blade Blaster!

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:04.170
Accel Synchro Monster?

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:12.180
Why did you protect your monster?

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:16.020
If you didn't do that, this 
duel wouldn't be over!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:23.120
I'm not willing to reveal all 
my Accel Synchro secrets.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.480
I'm looking forward to the day 
when we can duel again, Yusei.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:39.990
I promise to overcome my limits!

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:46.470
That's right.  I haven't 
overcome my limits yet.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:49.990
Accel Synchro will defeat the Meklords.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.360
I must find out how to do it.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:56.880
And who was that man in sunglasses?

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:03.790
I was found here.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:07.270
Where did I come from?

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:23.710
This place isn't for you.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.410
Who are you?

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.130
You're...

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.230
I won't let anyone interfere.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.560
That man...

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:36.890
Does he know who I am?

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.980
What do I know?

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:42.530
I feel that someone has given me a mission.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:15.680
Good.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.100
It's back to normal.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:19.590
Hey!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.910
We have to hurry.  Today is 
Team Unicorn's second match.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:28.560
They're facing our next 
opponent Team Catastrophe.

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:33.600
Yeah!  Let's watch Team Unicorn's 
battle and learn their strategies!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.690
Let's hurry to the stadium.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.890
They already started!

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.820
I hope Team Unicorn didn't win already!

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:54.960
What?  A crash?

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:56.490
What happened?

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:58.510
Look at that!

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.640
Jean!  Andore!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:08.440
Oh my goodness!  Team Unicorn!

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:14.400
The first and second 
wheelers have both crashed!

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:23.660
We thought Team Unicorn had the advantage 
in this duel, but Team Catastrophe won!

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:25.440
This must be a joke.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:30.130
I can't believe those two lost.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.880
That's Team Catastrophe.

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:12.940
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:17.950
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:22.850
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:27.860
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:32.730
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:39.670
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:43.510
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:49.380
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:53.280
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:59.220
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:02.190
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.460
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:09.100
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:11.970
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:15.440
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:18.680
At our special place
